              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iAI1Sh73GELMlgxKg"><p>As seasons change, it&apos;s important to adjust your routine to suit the weather. In winter, opt for richer moisturizers to combat dryness, while in summer, switch to lighter, oil-free options to manage sweat and oil production. During dry months, you may want to increase the use of hydrating serums or masks, whereas in humid seasons, focus more on controlling oil.</p></div></div
